  "body": "## What changed\n\n`SdfField::subtract_batch` (`field_cut.rs`) refused a chord when its swept window, clipped to the cut region, passed `MAX_CELLS_PER_MOVE` (1 << 22). A wide tool's own footprint can pass that count. Then a short move was refused, and segmenting could not help. The column engine cuts the same move.\n\nThe ceiling now bounds the cells that the chord's travel adds: the cells of the clipped window minus the cells of the same solid at rest at the chord's start, with the same reach, padding and clipping.\n\n- `Sweep::rest_window` (new, `field_sweep.rs`): the window of the solid with its path collapsed to its start. It lies inside `Sweep::window`. It is `None` for the lathe sweep, which keeps the old bound.\n- `window_of` now calls `window_between(sw, p0, p1, ...)`. The window of a chord is unchanged.\n- The refusal message names the new bound (\"... cells beyond the tool at rest ...\") and still asks the caller to segment the move.\n\nA short move of any tool passes. A long chord still refuses, and segmenting always brings it under the ceiling.\n\nNot changed: the f32 cut twin (`cut_twin_work.rs`, `TWIN_MAX_CELLS_PER_CHORD`) states the same value for its own work list. That is a follow-up if you want the two laws to stay the same.\n\n## Readings\n\nA 120 x 120 x 30 mm block at cell 0.254 mm, a flat tool 50.8 mm across, a feed at z 25:\n- A 1 mm move: refused before; cuts now. The faced top is air, and stock stays below the face and outside the tool.\n- A 120 mm chord: refused before and now.\n- The same chord in 24 pieces of 5 mm: cuts.\n\n## Pinning tests\n\n`crates/sim/tests/field_wide_tool.rs`, synthetic shapes only, 2 tests:\n- `a_wide_tools_short_move_cuts_on_the_field_engine_as_on_the_column_engine`: fails on the old code (refused on op 0).\n- `a_wide_tools_long_chord_still_refuses_and_its_segments_cut`.\n\nThe existing pin `an_unpayable_window_refuses_and_writes_nothing` (`stock_sdf_cut.rs`) still refuses. `stock_sdf_cut`, `stock_field_cost`, `field_arc_sweep` and `stock_backend_parity` pass.\n\n## Gates\n\nOn the final head `f9d231e63` (upstream/main merged in):\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green, 85 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 27.6 min.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `cargo xtask gate light`: green, 6 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 96.5 min (most of it the release build, on a shared box).\n- No heavy step: this is not a `P1` (work-issue section 3).\n\nThe decision is recorded in `docs/decisions/4079-wide-tool-ceiling.md`.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes (they run at the cut).\n- The GUI.\n\nEffort: high (stock simulation is under the safety floor).\nChangelog: Stock simulation: a wide tool's short move cuts on the field engine; before, the per-move cell ceiling refused it, and the column engine cut it.\n\nBranch: upstream/main merged in (plain merge); the diff is 4 files: `field_cut.rs`, `field_sweep.rs`, the new test file and the decision file.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nFixes #4079\n",
